 60TI c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL) January 4, 2026                  
 60TI c  {+60}Ti was produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility                        
 60TI2c  using the {+9}Be({+70}Zn,X) reaction at E=352 MeV/nucleon. Target was  
 60TI3c  8-mm thick {+9}Be. BigRIPS was tuned to optimize transmission of       
 60TI4c  {+55}Ca, which was incident on alternately a carbon target and a       
 60TI5c  target frame. The identification of the nuclide of interest was        
 60TI6c  made in the BigRIPS separator by determining the atomic number and the 
 60TI7c  mass-to-charge ratio of the ion using the tof-B|r-|DE method. The      
 60TI8c  reaction products were transported through the ZeroDegree Spectrometer 
 60TI9c  and implanted into the ZeroDegree Advanced Decay Station (ZD-ADS).     
 60TIac  The ZD-ADS is composed of an implantation detector, LaBr{-3} detectors,
 60TIbc  a neutron tof array and a veto detector. Measured: implanted           
 60TIcc  ion-|b{+-}-t, implanted ion-|b{+-}-|g-t and implanted ions-|g-t        
 60TIdc  correlations.                                                          
 60TIec  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
